    <string name="cal_how_title">How calendars work</string>
    <string name="cal_how_body">The widget can read events from two places.\n\nPhone calendars: calendars that apps sync into Android itself, like Google Calendar, the Xiaomi or Samsung calendar, Etar, DAVx⁵ or ICSx⁵.\n\nCalendar links: an .ics or webcal link to a calendar. Proton Calendar doesn’t share its events with Android, so this is the way to show them.\n\nPhone calendars update the widget as soon as they change. A link can’t tell the widget it changed, so it’s re-read every 10 minutes while you’re using the phone (and every 30 minutes otherwise), or straight away with Refresh now.</string>
